ven just rap music i  don't want to call it drilling in  vertical it's rap music in the end most  of them that are doing it they want a  way out but they also just want to be  heard tk wanted to be heard my man got  touched a subject now the first one mate  man the suspect tko up next  [Music]  left behind his girlfriend and their  unborn son  the day after his death she posted this  picture and wrote so grateful to be  carrying a part of you  this year's nottingham carnival was the  first in three years because of covid  two million people came to celebrate the  caribbean culture  but on the final day violence crept in  tk's was the first murder of the  festival in 18 years  it was a grim end to a largely  successful event  the organizers want to remind people of  that  you know it's hugely tragic and i don't  ever want to dismiss you know the life  that has been lost he's going he was  going to be a father you know there's a  huge tragedy you know but this this we  are not a monolith  you know we are many things and you know  what happened to him happened after the  masqueraders are pretty much done as  well this is not a reflection of who we  are actually what happened to him is the  opposite of who we are  it's four days on from the murder  tk's blood stains remain on the pavement  where he was attacked  his family are traveling to london  because they need to formally identify  their son's body  how are you doing i join them as they  visit the scene of his killing for the  first time  i'm so sorry  about your son  and could you just tell us a bit about  him  well he was a normal good kid  yeah just came to carnival to enjoy  himself with um with his sister  the sister i just take out the car about  to have fun  then what happened his life was just  taken away  i can't imagine what it's been like you  for the family  well as  with any family who lost a child like  that it's gonna be devastated so it's  hard you know i mean it's hard to carry  on because he's our son and we love him  really he loves us he's got good heart  clean-hearted kid and i mean  just want to do good  that's about it  could you tell me um the moment that you  got the phone call that you realized he  was in some trouble well i was  devastated  i was devastated i was just praying that  he was okay but everything was gonna be  fine  but obviously  work that  and um did you go to the hospital i did  yeah i did  what would you say to any kids who are  thinking about picking up a knife  well i would say  that's the wrong thing to do yeah  you are not going around and trying to  hurt other people you need to show love  love is the answer love is the key if  everybody should love then no one will  hurt each other you hurt each other  so that's all we need to do to show love  and once you have love then you won't be  carrying nothing  his plea for peace comes during the  worst surge of violence in england since  last year  which was the worst on record  in the last 12 months knife crime in the  capital has gone up by more than 10  percent  and it's accelerated even more in the  last month  more than a week after tk's murder  there's still been no arrests  i've come to meet a murder detective  who's just retired from the met  i asked him what clues investigators  will be looking for  in this particular case you have  somebody who's involved in drill music  and rap music and  and there is always that  element where drill music has that  unfortunate  notability for being something where  violence and serious violence and murder  and possession of guns and knives has  been glorified really  and and so that the music will be looked  into as well and the lyrics you know  it's quite common that  that is a theme that you look at when  you have a victim or a suspect in in a  case like this that there may be clues  within that that drill music in the  lyrics and that's been used in many  court cases in the last really 10 years  knife crime and knife killings this is  so